In Classic WoW, most warlocks were seen with voidwalkers because **voidwalkers were the default pet for leveling**—they were easier to obtain (learned at level 10), more durable, and provided essential utility like *Sacrifice* (for tanking damage) and *Consume Shadows* (for safe out-of-combat healing). While the succubus was stronger DPS-wise, she required a higher-level spell (*Summon Succubus*, learned at level 40) and was more fragile, making her less ideal for early leveling and solo questing. [end of text]


